{"title":"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems\">2002 AMC 12A #16</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">2002 AMC 10A #24</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Cheese)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution-_Quick,_Easy_Method\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution- Quick, Easy Method</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tina randomly selects two distinct numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9fc022f97b5efa851a01ef6ef421a8d3acd7a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, and Sergio randomly selects a number from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee6cb2c8d80deaf1dbc0df782ef84cc29bb1942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 1, 2, ..., 10 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />. What is the probability that Sergio's number is larger than the sum of the two numbers chosen by Tina? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/c/0cc562f978eb58e4e64e5d7c92b0c4eeccd98b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2/5 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 9/20 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 1/2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 11/20 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 24/25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This is not too bad using casework. \n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 3: This happens in only one way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb913ad463dcc2916d4135977f0d06f20ad93cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and Sergio can choose a number from 4 to 10, inclusive. There are 7 ways that Sergio gets a desirable number here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 4: This once again happens in only one way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b6a9f4b07be4cb5a24874bb192da96ca853ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Sergio can choose a number from 5 to 10, so 6 ways here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 5: This can happen in two ways <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c05a83f0a33c3f141fbfb48c803d0e906974e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876b66789c31005ef23e41081d8f7c10137faaa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Sergio can choose a number from 6 to 10, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe05e8a7e0d075708f5a5fbbf0f841551ba38057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot5=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> ways here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 6: Two ways here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f46e8ad13e4a3e569bb6c47d1d642243a3119d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f4d1e83d6eef61f31d78844deb189c54a7abc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Sergio can choose a number from 7 to 10, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f2aab8c71f7caee70a3e1cd0db136459243229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot4=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 7: Two ways here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9d3308a17610dcb38bfd84b443bdd0ea403605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97fadfe6bdbd1adb164f263b52f2a290723ad45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Sergio can choose from 8 to 10, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec53f7be728ae20c9dabca93474181a913ea808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot3=6$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> ways here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 8: Only one way possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/564a0113de9b4ac87eeb5fa411e0937162315e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />). Sergio chooses 9 or 10, so 2 ways here.\n</p><p>Tina gets a sum of 9: Only one way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc04892c672addda50fb21cd723f160be2443f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Sergio must choose 10, so 1 way.\n</p><p>In all, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd851df91c3cc471029c06ca69a73eafc555569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+6+10+8+6+2+1=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"248\" height=\"14\" /> ways. Tina chooses two distinct numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee559317aed18491b8093c9dffcc7931e41f1991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{2}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> ways while Sergio chooses a number in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b085668dbec5f7ac7ce468298ca36deca25cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot 10=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> ways in all. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f1d8875587f32ba55d179e16e2b16536c7bb96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{100}=\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/36385e908426e3a89be2996eec033d15df861f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A)}\\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"50\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We invoke some symmetry. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> denote Tina's sum, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote Sergio's number. Observe that, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c99072191bc33b741343e05328472c55b19608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 2, 3, \\ldots, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acffef64b1c46a92481bbe62a341f8ffe5ece15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Pr}(T=i) = \\text{Pr}(T=12-i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If Tina's sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, then the probability that Sergio's number is larger than Tina's sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da6ff8ead6f5ce401d32c7dd70df7568a720655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10-i}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f24ff01ce8e35402fec7f992bbec8fa146f333c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = \\text{Pr}(S&gt;T) = \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=i) \\times \\frac{10-i}{10}\\]\" width=\"319\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Using the symmetry observation, we can also write the above sum as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f197fc9994b16873f3169a391ef2f1242b263017.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=12-i) \\times \\frac{10-i}{10} = \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=i) \\times \\frac{i-2}{10}\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"50\" />\nwhere the last equality follows as we reversed the indices of the sum (by replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1506008537f6da4236d2f32d3584a535738f2b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />). Thus, adding the two equivalent expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf12211f7b003811deac24ec1d62aa1764a2c88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2P &amp;= \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=i) \\times \\left(\\frac{10-i}{10} + \\frac{i-2}{10}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=i) \\times \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{4}{5} \\sum_{i=2}^{10} \\text{Pr}(T=i) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{4}{5} \\end{align*}\" width=\"310\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p>Since this represents twice the desired probability, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc0cef2d523584cf7d5d36be13d95b1b34cdb3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"92\" height=\"48\" />. -scrabbler94\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have 4 cases, if Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1283d75b15dbe0ae16f4c102b89f3ab767fdcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and always chooses numbers greater than the first number she chose.\n</p><p>The number of ways of choosing 2 numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/53130d1c08583295cd18d9042920935e82bae549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Case 1: Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, since the numbers are distinct, Tina can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d2979bdee65809caa2c3c11136db79a912e4ad28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994cd14ccf0cd9e6dca73b0673ca4f322ec73d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sergio only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca23217407e3615b4c90fbb9a1fde93d8456e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-3=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> choices.\n</p><p>Since the sum of the combined numbers increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every time for this specific case, Sergio has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less choice every time.\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d2259cf6932b6e5c3a45dfe617d98c4778d8985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7+6+5+4}{10 \\cdot \\binom{5}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"105\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Case 2: Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, Tina can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfacccde7e7e27fee19340cc246f8d8856da67c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3), (2, 4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463af35503b7a81d0c672a8fe461c185378bcd0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 5).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>If Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sergio only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866e1c43d88d717b496c171f965e35bb782cee1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-5=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> choices.\n</p><p>Since the sum of the combined numbers increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every time for this specific case, Sergio has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less choice every time.\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a89de1ae9e3a4084f71b729308dbe0a0656b6bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5+4+3}{10 \\cdot \\binom{5}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"78\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Case 3: Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, Tina can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892bfe5fc4ddb9515562db432b77b5cc1b13aecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b383072fa1f491732a33254bdd706582e58bbcb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>If Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sergio only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea7c9bccd0fe3c94d33f6a2c4ccbb93a5b51707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-7=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> choices.\n</p><p>Since the sum of the combined numbers increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every time for this specific case, Sergio has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less choice every time.\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48ce4a1ced14adc3954851353635741795ca38e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3+2}{10 \\cdot \\binom{5}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"60\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Case 4: Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, Tina can only choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfabbb531c2b249507fb05072d1771f1436e3c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,5).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If Tina chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sergio only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5a12b62b6d5eaac5a6279d4d9971e27aeb2e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-9=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> choice.\n</p><p>Therefore, the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c3879092e2594f2cb946a70bb25cdaaa1ac7b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10 \\cdot \\binom{5}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"60\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Once you add these probabilities up, you will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c423c5641d01830bc1cf66910568932e9588aec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(7+6+5+4)+(5+4+3)+(3+2)+(1)}{10 \\cdot\\binom{5}{2}} = \\frac{40}{100} = \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"446\" height=\"48\" /> probability.\n</p><p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Assume Sergio chooses from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cba7448f562cfd148ecbeeb3bdd81a9e13fd920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2,3,\\ldots,10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. The probability of Tina getting a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179631a9be3047af0432ea70d1fe200ff4f4577b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> and a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b2e3749f140d8825e7aa6225b1c0511b6be450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863c54dbe16fb785b4e4578b547435dd48b367cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, are equal due to symmetry. The probability of Sergio choosing numbers higher/lower than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179631a9be3047af0432ea70d1fe200ff4f4577b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to him choosing numbers lower/higher than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b2e3749f140d8825e7aa6225b1c0511b6be450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore over all of Tina's sums, the probability of Sergio choosing a number higher is equal to the probability of choosing a number lower. \n</p><p>The probability that they get the same value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3dba22edcee4ff7213635505e90128beebb42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />, so the probability of Sergio getting a higher number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a37cadbc59f3fff75312977a38aa2db2a2d4ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(9-1)/2}{9} = \\frac49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Sergio never wins when choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049a0bb81a046e19c7d06139c95de8071cea9ab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac49 \\cdot \\frac{9}{10} + (0)\\frac{1}{10} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\frac{2}{5}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"201\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~zeric\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 5 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>List all the cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3069e19b2672a257e38bc79d35d6855ef2d78e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\in [1, 10]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5095ebbbbd418bd528383b8c02e10f1e59e8b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0+0+0+1+2+4+6+8+9+10}{\\binom{5}{2} \\cdot 10} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"384\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Cheese)\">Solution 6 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Add up the first set and then divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Multiply this by two and you can see the expected value of the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance you will get a number higher this is great if you are running low on time.\n</p><p>(Note: this method only works because Tina's largest value (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) is less than Sergio's (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />). If Sergio chose a random number from a set like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930990a1fc169b86f182c5d855c477c2f01c99e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />, this method gives an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e183a6c68f486e1333dcc47a8211a6eec77c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14.3 \\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> whereas the actual answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c1bbe6ab11377a284f67f70a29786081f9edbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18.6 \\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />.)\n</p><p>~notgarv\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8WrdYLw9_ns?t=381\">https://youtu.be/8WrdYLw9_ns?t=381</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZdZt9uzyMME\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZdZt9uzyMME</a>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution-_Quick.2C_Easy_Method\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution-_Quick,_Easy_Method\">Video Solution- Quick, Easy Method</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution- Quick, Easy Method\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQ1EsX5JzoI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQ1EsX5JzoI</a> \n</p><p>~Solution by Math Katana\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A\" title=\"2